Abstract Design Pattern
It is creational design pattern used to create objects of related type without specifying their concreate classes.
Why do we need it:
when your system needs to create multiple related objects together
ensure consistency (object belog to same family avoid multiple if-else)
In this pattern client does not directly create objects using new instead it interacts with an abstract factory interface.
  Ex:
      we have 2 type of objects:
                    Shape likes Circle and Rectangle
                    Color like Red and Blue
      Instead of creating objects using new keyword, we create factories. One factory is responsible for shapes, and another for colors
      First, client ask for factory using FactoryProducer, then using that asks for Shape or Color
      This way client does not know the actual classes and interact with interfaces only.

                  1: we choose factory
                  2: that factory create related objects
